.TH MCS 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mcs \- write an Intel-HEX (.mcs) FPGA image to a card's configuration PROM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcs
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-\-swap\-data ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I devnum mcs_file
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens
.BI /dev/pcidev devnum
(created by the
.B pci_devel_main
module, not by
.BR mu2e (4))
and programs the PROM from the Intel-HEX records of
.IR mcs_file :
it computes the block range, erases it, then writes the data records.
Normally run through
.BR mcs.sh (1),
which unloads
.B mu2e
first.
The usage text omits the
.I devnum
operand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-e
Erase only, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-swap\-data
Byte-swap the data words.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-?
Usage, exit 0.
.TP
.B \-V
RCS revision, exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on completion; 255 (\-1) if fewer than two operands.
A failed open of the device is reported
.RB ( "open: ..." )
but not fatal \(em the program continues with an invalid descriptor;
a missing
.I mcs_file
is not checked before
.BR fscanf (3).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Forces
.B TRACE_LVLS
to 0xf if unset and enables TRACE memory+slow output.
.SH FILES
.BI /dev/pcidev N
.SH WARNINGS
Rewrites FPGA firmware; a power cycle is needed afterwards.
No confirmation is asked.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
sudo mcs.sh 0 DTC_v2025.mcs
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcs.sh (1),
.BR devl (1),
.BR mu2e (4)
